KKBP

KKBP is licensed under the MIT License (LICENSE). It continues the legacy KKBP importer and
exporters; the credits below are for the work it ports or reproduces.

The legacy KKBP importer
  Copyright (c) 2024 KKBP developers. MIT License.
  The Rigify Hook's scripts (importer/kkbp/builtin/rigify/before.py, after.py and commons.py) are
  its Rigify scripts, ported with as few changes as possible. The Material Template library and the
  built-in Hooks' asset files (importer/kkbp/library/) are built from its KK Shader V9.blend
  (importer/templates-src/), which holds the shader templates, the edit templates, the Rigify
  widgets, the face-card rig and its mouth atlas, and the outline materials.

The legacy exporters
  The KKBP Exporter for Koikatsu (originally by Sonogami-Rinne and MediaMoots) and the Summer 
  Vacation Scramble Character Exporter (Sonogami-Rinne under LGPL-3.0) were the reference 
  for the new exporters, such as where the light is placed for the light and dark bakes. 
  The new exporters are new code and bundle nothing from them.

The importer also rewrites, as its own code, features that the legacy importer took from these
projects. No code from them is bundled; their work was the reference.

Material Combiner
  https://github.com/Grim-es/material-combiner-addon
  Copyright (c) 2018 shotariya. MIT License.
  The export atlas (importer/kkbp/atlas/ and importer/kkbp/tools/export_prep/atlas.py) reproduces
  its layout, image tiling and UV remapping.

  It used Jake Gordon's binary-tree bin packer:
  Copyright (c) 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016 Jake Gordon and contributors. MIT License.
  importer/kkbp/atlas/layout.py follows the same algorithm.

Cats Blender Plugin
  https://github.com/michaeldegroot/cats-blender-plugin
  Copyright (c) 2017 GiveMeAllYourCats. MIT License.
  The Merge Weights tool (importer/kkbp/tools/merge_weights.py) reproduces its Merge Weights.

KKShadersRecreated and KKShadersPlus
  https://github.com/xukmi/KKShadersPlus
  Copyright (c) 2021 xukmi. MIT License (as KKShadersRecreated's LICENSE states).
  The edit materials' shadow colours (importer/kkbp/shading/) follow their recreation of the
  game's ShadeAdjustItem and MapValuesMain, which the legacy importer had translated.

The joint-correction drivers in the Rigify Hook (importer/kkbp/builtin/rigify/prepare.py) come
mostly from a .blend file by johnbbob_la_petite on the Koikatsu Discord, as in the legacy importer.

